<title>USA: Union Acceptance stake taken by U.K. group.</title>
<headline>Union Acceptance stake taken by U.K. group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including Mercury Asset Management Plc, a London-based investment firm, said Thursday it has acquired 205,000 class A common shares or 5.11 percent stake of the class outstanding.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it bought the shares between September 19 and october 21 at prices ranging from $16.875 to $19.328 a share.</p>
<p>The group said it holds the stake in the Indianapolis, Ind.,-based personal credit institution for investment purposes.</p>
</text>
